-- Source module: Solutions.KFMGlue
/-!
# KFM 1: the final reduction with a raised threshold and a polylog slack factor

`Glue.kappaBound_of_machine` asks for `time ≤ C₀ (V · Ncost + n)` for **every** `n ≥ n₀`
(`n₀ = 2^{2^{2^{132}}}`).  The IL machine (MACHINE-PLAN.md, item 4) misses this literal shape in
two harmless ways:

* its cost carries extra factors polynomial in `log p` (row-addition constant `CR ∝ K`,
  `log_m D` recursion depths, `log Z` descriptor sizes), and
* some side conditions (e.g. `80 Z (Z+2) ≤ 2^K` of `KFR.rowHyp_of_lem13`) hold only for
  `n ≥ n₁` with `n₁` far above `n₀`.

Both fit in the slack of Table 1: `Ncost ≤ 50 p^{1-2κ}` (`RCost.Ncost_le`) while the target is
`n lg^{1-κ}`.  This file proves

* **`kappaBound_of_machine_slack`**: a correct machine with
  `time ≤ C₀ (V · Ncost · F n + n)` for `n ≥ max n₀ n₁`, where `0 ≤ F n ≤ (6 lg n)^κ`, satisfies
  `KappaBound (2⁻¹⁸²)`;
* **`polylog_slack`**: for every `A` and `c`, eventually `c (log(6 lg n) + 1)^A ≤ (6 lg n)^κ`,
  so any fixed power of `log p` is an admissible `F`;
* **`kappaBound_of_machine_polylog`**: the combination, with `F n = c (log(6 lg n)+1)^A` and an
  arbitrary threshold `n₁`.
-/

namespace NLogN.KFM

open IntMul.OpenAI.Glue IntMul.OpenAI.RCost

noncomputable section

/-- `lg n → ∞`. -/
lemma lg_ge (B : ℕ) : ∀ n, 2 ^ B ≤ n → B ≤ IntMul.lg n := by
  intro n hn
  have h := Nat.clog_mono_right 2 hn
  rw [Nat.clog_pow 2 B (by norm_num)] at h
  exact h.trans (le_max_left _ _)

end

end NLogN.KFM

end

